# fixedbugs, defect 2053, 2026-10-13, the function never called, its words
# the Windows target's: judged there alone
# (`tests/harness/platform_skips.hero`), and its mark on every platform.
#
# SYMPTOM: on the Windows box (clang 23.1.1, MSVC target) a header of the
# program's own defining `hero_str_len` again as `static` built and ran at
# exit 0 where the program never calls it, a unit giving one name both
# linkages, which C11 6.2.2p7 leaves undefined.
#
# FIX: `-Wmicrosoft-redeclare-static` is an error in the header's region
# (`emit/header_region.hero`'s `EXTENDED`), so Windows refuses the header at
# its line 5, exit 1, its note told as the Heroes runtime's own name.

extern "fixedbugs-2053-a-header-that-defines-an-uncalled-runtime-function-again-as-static-is-refused-on-windows.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    print(eight())
